From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:35:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/44] Camera: the off-hand list's item held in the left hand

A game can give a player an "offhand" inventory list; its first item is
drawn in first person in the left hand, next to the wielded one, in the
same wield scene, so it never shows in third person. It is lowered at
the bottom left and goes up beside the crosshair while the item's meta
field "raised" is "1", in 0.2 s (eased, rotation slerped). It rises into
view when it changes and sways and bobs as the right hand, mirrored,
but stays still while digging.

goodluckOS's shield mod copies the worn 3d_armor shield there and sets
"raised" while it is held up, which on a gamepad had no other way to
show (a HUD image also covered the third person view). The poses are
settings (offhand_position, offhand_rotation, offhand_raised_position,
offhand_raised_rotation), tuned at 640x480 with the 72 degree wield
camera.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/builtin/settingtypes.txt b/builtin/settingtypes.txt
index 9319e3a0d..b88b4ec4c 100644
--- a/builtin/settingtypes.txt
+++ b/builtin/settingtypes.txt
@@ -526,6 +526,14 @@ undersampling (Undersampling) int 1 1 8
 #    the arm when the camera moves.
 arm_inertia (Arm inertia) bool true
 
+#    Where the item of the player's "offhand" inventory list (a shield) is held in
+#    first person: position and rotation in degrees, lowered and raised (while its
+#    meta field "raised" is "1").
+offhand_position (Off-hand position) v3f (-41, -32, 65)
+offhand_rotation (Off-hand rotation) v3f (0, -25, 0)
+offhand_raised_position (Raised off-hand position) v3f (-22, -18, 50)
+offhand_raised_rotation (Raised off-hand rotation) v3f (0, 10, 0)
+
 #    Enable view bobbing and amount of view bobbing.
 #    For example: 0 for no view bobbing; 1.0 for normal; 2.0 for double.
 view_bobbing_amount (View bobbing factor) float 1.0 0.0 7.9
